# Host keys for the public pairing hop, pinned by this repository.
#
# ssh verifies the endpoint against this file and nothing else. utils/tunnel.py
# passes UserKnownHostsFile pointing here and empties GlobalKnownHostsFile, so
# neither ~/.ssh/known_hosts nor the system store can decide what the tunnel
# trusts: an earlier unverified connection, another program running as this user
# or an interception on first use stays out of the decision.
#
# Both lines were scanned from the live endpoint on 2026-11-20 and checked, by
# fingerprint, against the two the endpoint publishes for its key types and
# against the SHA-256 SSHFP records signed in DNS for the same host.
# tests/test_mobile_public_tunnel.py carries the two fingerprints, so a rotated
# key is a deliberate edit here and never an acceptance on first use.
#
# To rotate a key: scan the new one, compare its fingerprint against both sources
# over a channel that is not the connection being verified, and commit the line
# only when they agree. A key matching neither is an interception; the tunnel
# stays refused and the product says so.

localhost.run ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAILVqOuSMnyeGDVO1lG6EaG5In/dXABCchhmHKkuRU2s9
localhost.run ssh-rsa 
